                    VIBRANCE SOFTWARE PRIVACY POLICY
                      Last Updated: 28 August, 2026

  Team Vibrance ("we", "our", "us") is committed to maintaining trust
and transparency with our users. We want to disclose different types of
information on how we collect, use, and protect your information when
using our software application Vibrance (the "Software").

  By downloading, installing, or using the Software, you agree to the
collection and use of information in compliance with this policy.

1. INFORMATION WE COLLECT
- Personal Data: 
During the testing phase of the Software, we require you to authenticate 
via a third-party service like Discord to verify eligibility and manage 
access for our early-testing community.

By logging in with Discord, you authorise us to access your avatar, username,
and user ID to confirm eligibility during this early-testing phase. 

Please note that authenticating with Discord is a temporary requirement
exclusive only to the testing period; upon the full commercial release of
the Software, authentication with Discord will become optional.

- Automatically Collected Data:
When using our software, we automatically collect technical data, device type,
hardware, operating system version, and crash logs.

2. HOW WE USE YOUR INFORMATION
- To ensure the stability and functional integrity of the Software.
- To verify and manage access to the Software during its testing period.
- To improve user experience, conduct analytics, and troubleshoot technical bugs.
- To send critical updates, security alerts, and support messages.

3. DATA SHARING AND DISCLOSURE
We will never, ever, sell your personal data. We do not need it, nor have
the intent to use the information we receive. We only use the information
we collect to improve user experience with our Software. We will only share
certain information we collect with current and potential third-party
service providers that assists with operating the Software or when it is
required by law.

4. DATA SECURITY
We only store information that contains your Discord avatar, username,
and user ID. This also includes telemetry linked to your device such as your
Graphics Processing Unit (GPU), Central Processing Unit (CPU), Random Access
Memory (RAM), and your Operating System (OS). Any confidential personal
information such as e-mail, passwords, banking information, or anything
related will never be stored in our database.

5. YOUR RIGHTS AS A USER
Depending where you are in the world, you may have the right to access, amend,
and request deletion of any personal data related to you.

6. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY
We may update this privacy policy occasionally. We will notify you of any
changes by posting the policy within the software interface or via our
Discord server link below.

